WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
This demonstration uses real Oracle and Bedrock
services with three synthetic policies.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Titan creates embeddings, Oracle retrieves
evidence, and Nova generates a cited answer.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000
The application is local; the database and model
calls run in the cloud.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Titan Text Embeddings V2 creates document and
question vectors.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Amazon Nova Lite generates answers from the
retrieved evidence.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Nova Lite also generates bounded SQL. This is
not database-side Select AI.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Select a policy question in the browser
application.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Click Run live RAG to call Bedrock and Oracle.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.000
The choices cover transfers, warranties,
recycling, and missing evidence.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.000
The Python code invokes Titan Text Embeddings
version two through the AWS SDK.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.000
It requests one thousand twenty-four dimensions
and validates the returned vector.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:12.000
The same embedding model processes every
document and each new question.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:18.000
This is the SQL actually executed by the live
demonstration.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:24.000
Bound documents become vectors; Oracle orders
them by exact cosine distance.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:30.000
A temporary CLOB holds the large payload. No
persistent tables are changed.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:36.000
This Converse call uses the configured Nova Lite
model.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:42.000
The prompt contains the question and the chunks
returned by Oracle.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:48.000
The system instruction requests citations and
rejects unsupported answers.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:54.000
This capture shows the result returned by the
live browser application.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:02:00.000
The transfer policy ranks first and supplies the
thirty-seven-hour approval requirement.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:06.000
The evidence text and distance are visible, so
you can inspect the citation.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:12.000
The sensor warranty question retrieves a
different document as the top result.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:18.000
Its eighteen-month answer is supported by the
displayed warranty policy.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:24.000
Each click calls the services again; these are
not prewritten application answers.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:30.000
Project Aspen has no policy in this deliberately
small document fixture.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:36.000
Inspect the live response instead of accepting a
borrowed policy for another project.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:42.000
This example is a useful check, not a
comprehensive hallucination evaluation.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:48.000
Ask for the top three inventory items with risk
at least seventy.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:54.000
Nova Lite returns SQL; review it before allowing
execution.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:03:00.000
The model identifier and Bedrock request ID are
visible.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:06.000
The server accepts only one complete SELECT
grammar.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:12.000
It extracts two integers and executes this fixed
query with binds.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:18.000
Raw model SQL never reaches Oracle. The
transaction is read-only.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:24.000
Click Run reviewed SELECT after inspecting the
generated statement.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:30.000
Oracle returns three synthetic items with scores
ninety-two, eighty-one, and seventy-four.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:36.000
Rows come directly from Oracle, without model
summarization.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:42.000
Change the minimum risk to eighty-five and
generate again.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:48.000
Review and run the new SQL. Only one fixture row
qualifies.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:54.000
The five-row fixture is synthetic, not business
inventory.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:04:00.000
With a minimum risk of ninety-five, Oracle
returns no rows.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:06.000
The model does not invent a matching product.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:12.000
Unsupported write requests are rejected before
database execution.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:18.000
Install requirements and configure private
Oracle and AWS access.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:24.000
Run the smoke test, start the app, and open its
loopback URL.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:30.000
For SQL, generate, review, then run. Both flows
use real cloud services.
